WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.398
stretto.

2
00:00:01.398 --> 00:00:02.956
Read ahead of your agent.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.085
An agent spends an LLM turn on every tool call,

4
00:00:09.085 --> 00:00:11.753
and those turns are most of what it costs.

5
00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:16.465
But many of those turns are decided before they start.

6
00:00:16.465 --> 00:00:18.612
The first result named both orders,

7
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:22.722
so the next two reads were fixed by the tools, not by the customer.

8
00:00:24.122 --> 00:00:26.848
stretto makes those reads for the agent.

9
00:00:26.848 --> 00:00:31.345
They ride in the same tool result, so the agent skips those turns.

10
00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:36.251
A wrong read costs only tokens, and changes nothing: stretto only reads.

11
00:00:37.651 --> 00:00:38.656
First, record.

12
00:00:38.656 --> 00:00:41.169
stretto-proxy wraps any MCP server,

13
00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:44.687
forwards every message, and records each session.

14
00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:46.791
Then learn.

15
00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:51.976
stretto counts which reads follow which calls, and where each argument came from.

16
00:00:51.976 --> 00:00:54.537
The flow is a file you review like code.

17
00:00:55.937 --> 00:00:56.643
Then serve.

18
00:00:56.643 --> 00:01:01.653
After each call, the flow's lookups ride in the result the agent already gets.

19
00:01:01.653 --> 00:01:04.286
No new tool, and no change to the prompt.

20
00:01:05.686 --> 00:01:13.991
A lookup is made when the chance that the agent uses it before its next write clears a threshold set by costs, about 0.3.

21
00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:16.462
No model is asked: the proxy counts.

22
00:01:17.962 --> 00:01:26.418
Live, on 28 τ²-bench retail and airline tasks, GLM-5.3 took 27.9% fewer LLM turns.

23
00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:30.440
In AgentDojo's Slack and travel suites,

24
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:37.555
GLM-5.3 and Claude Haiku 4.5 took 10.1% fewer, with passes unchanged.

25
00:01:38.955 --> 00:01:41.970
To start, install stretto and run stretto init.

26
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.331
It prints your host's configuration, and the steps to a served flow.

27
00:01:46.331 --> 00:01:49.346
The quickstart runs the whole loop with no key.

28
00:01:50.946 --> 00:01:51.444
stretto.

29
00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.002
Read ahead of your agent.
